{% doc %}
  Links to every real, non-empty, non-frontpage collection, plus "All" —
  the actual mechanism behind "filter by collection." Shopify's storefront
  filters (collection.filters) can only filter by tag, type, price,
  availability, variant option, or metafield — there's no "which
  collection" facet, because you're already inside one when using it.
  Jumping to a different collection is ordinary navigation between
  collection.url values, not a query param, so this renders plain links.

  frontpage is excluded on purpose: it's the homepage's curated collection,
  not a customer-facing category. Every other published, non-empty
  collection shows automatically — nothing to configure when a new one is
  added.

  Rendered twice: as the standalone row above the collection toolbar, and
  again inside the Filter panel, so both stay in sync from one place.

  @param {collection} current - the collection currently being viewed
  @example
  {% render 'category-pills', current: collection %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- assign other_collections_count = 0 -%}
{%- for cat in collections -%}
  {%- unless cat.handle == 'frontpage' or cat.products_count == 0 -%}
    {%- assign other_collections_count = other_collections_count | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if other_collections_count > 0 -%}
  <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="category-pills__link{% if current.handle == 'all' %} is-active{% endif %}">All</a>
  {%- for cat in collections -%}
    {%- unless cat.handle == 'frontpage' or cat.products_count == 0 -%}
      <a href="{{ cat.url }}" class="category-pills__link{% if cat.handle == current.handle %} is-active{% endif %}">{{ cat.title }}</a>
    {%- endunless -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
